### Part 2: Code ka Line-by-Line Dry Run (Teeno Cases)

Ab dekhte hain code mein step-by-step memory mein kya bana aur kya badla:

#### Case 1: Primitive (`int number = 10;`)

* **`main` ke Stack mein:** `number = 10`.
* **`changePrimitive(number)` call hua:** Stack mein ek naya box bana `changePrimitive` ke liye. `number` ki value (`10`) ki ek **copy** bankar `x` mein gayi (`x = 10`).
* **`x = 99;` chala:** Sirf `changePrimitive` wale box ke andar `x` badal kar `99` hua. `main` wale box ka `number` abhi bhi `10` hi hai.
* Method khatam -> `x` wala box delete.
* **Output:** `10`.

---

#### Case 2: Array Element Change (`changeArrayElement(scores)`)

* **`int[] scores = {10, 20, 30};` chala:**
* **Heap mein** address `@101` par ek array bana: `[10, 20, 30]`.
* **`main` ke Stack mein:** `scores = @101` store hua (yani `scores` ke paas sirf address hai).


* **`changeArrayElement(scores)` call hua:**
* Naya Stack box bana `changeArrayElement` ke liye.
* Java **Pass-by-Value** hai, isliye `scores` ke andar jo value thi (`@101`), uski ek **copy** `arr` ko mili (`arr = @101`).
* Ab `scores` aur `arr` dono ke paas **same address `@101**` hai!


* **`arr[0] = 99;` chala:**
* `arr` address `@101` par gaya (Heap mein) aur uske 0th index ko `10` se `99` kar diya.
* Heap mein `@101` par rakha array ab `[99, 20, 30]` ho chuka hai.


* Method khatam -> `arr` wala Stack box delete, par Heap mein change ho chuka hai!
* **Output:** `[99, 20, 30]`.

---

#### Case 3: Reassignment Trap (`reassignArray(scores)`) — Sabse Important!

* **`reassignArray(scores)` call hua:**
* Naya Stack box bana `reassignArray` ke liye.
* Phir se `scores` ke address (`@101`) ki ek **copy** `arr` ko mili (`arr = @101`).


* **`arr = new int[]{500, 600, 700};` chala:**
* `new` keyword chalte hi **Heap mein** ek bilkul naya array bana, maan lo address **`@202`** par: `[500, 600, 700]`.
* Aur `arr = ...` likhne se sirf `reassignArray` ke local variable `arr` ka address badal kar `@101` se **`@202`** ho gaya!
* **`main` ke Stack mein `scores` ke paas abhi bhi purana address `@101` hi hai!**


* Method khatam -> `reassignArray` ka box delete (aur `@202` wala naya array bekaar hokar Garbage Collector ke liye chhoot gaya).
* Jab `main` mein `Arrays.toString(scores)` chala, toh woh apne address `@101` par gaya, jahan abhi bhi **`[99, 20, 30]`** rakha hai!

