### Do Classic Shift Traps Jo Interview Mein Fasate Hain

1. **Shift Count Wrap-Around (`% 32` aur `% 64`):**
Java mein `int` par shift karte waqt shift count ka sirf lower **5 bits** (`shiftCount & 31`, yaani `shiftCount % 32`) use hota hai; `long` ke liye lower **6 bits** (`shiftCount % 64`). Isliye `1 << 32` `0` nahi deta—`32 % 32 = 0` maankar `1 << 0` = **`1`** deta hai.
2. **Small Type Promotion (`byte`, `short`, `char`):**
Shift karne se pehle bhi ye `int` mein promote hote hain, isliye result `int` (ya `long` agar operand `long` ho) aata hai.

Agar ye teeno operators (`<<`, `>>`, `>>>`) aur `% 32` wala rule samajh aa gaya hai, toh shift questions aaram se handle ho jaayenge.


