Is poore page mein se tere kaam ki cheez bas **core behavior traps, shortcuts, aur common mistakes** hain. Baaki basic syntax (`+`, `-`, `&&`, `||`, ternary) pehle se jaana-pehchana hai—uspar time kharch karne ki zaroorat nahi hai.

### 1. Sabse Kaam Ki Baatein (High-Signal Traps)

* **Integer Division Truncation (`10 / 3 == 3`):** Jab dono operands `int` hon, division decimal nahi deta—zero ki taraf truncate karta hai (`3.33` nahi, `3`). Decimal chahiye toh kam se kam ek operand `double` ya `float` hona chahiye (`10.0 / 3`).
* **Prefix vs. Postfix (`++a` vs `a++`):** `a++` pehle purani value expression mein deta hai aur baad mein badhata hai; `++a` pehle badhata hai aur phir nayi value deta hai. Ek hi expression mein same variable ko baar-baar `++`/`--` karne se bachna chahiye—readable aur bug-free code ke liye alag lines mein likhna behtar hai.
* **Compound Assignment Implicit Cast (`+=`, `-=`, etc.):** Maan le `byte b = 10;` hai. Agar tu `b = b + 5;` likhega toh error aayega (kyunki `b + 5` ka type `int` banta hai), lekin `b += 5;` chal jaata hai kyunki compound assignment mein implicit narrowing cast hoti hai.
* **Short-Circuit (`&&` aur `||`):** `&&` mein pehla part `false` ho toh aage ka code evaluate hi nahi hota; `||` mein pehla part `true` ho toh aage ka skip ho jaata hai. Isse `null` checks safe bante hain (jaise `obj != null && obj.isValid()`).
* **Ternary Type Rules (`?:`):** Dono branches (`expression1` aur `expression2`) ka compatible type hona zaroori hai—warna type mismatch/boxing traps aa sakte hain.
* **`instanceof` Basics:** Reference type check karta hai (`obj instanceof Integer`). `null` par `instanceof` hamesha `false` deta hai (`null instanceof Integer` -> `false`, `NullPointerException` nahi aata).

### 2. "Common Mistakes to Avoid" Ka Real Meaning

* **`=` vs `==`:** `=` assignment hai, `==` comparison hai (`boolean` condition mein `=` daalne par syntax error aata hai).
* **Float `==` Precision:** Floating-point math (`0.1 + 0.2`) binary representation ki wajah se exact decimal nahi hoti, isliye `==` ke bajaye epsilon/tolerance ya `BigDecimal` (money/exact decimals ke liye) socha jaata hai.
* **String `==` vs `.equals()`:** `==` reference/address compare karta hai, `.equals()` actual text content compare karta hai.
* **Precedence:** Jab expression confusing lage, parenthesis `()` laga kar intent clear rakho—interviewer ko precedence table yaad hone se zyada clarity pasand aati hai.

